ons.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressions to Show Interest", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use these phrases and techniques to show interest and  surprise in conversation:<br>  <br><ul><li>Use rising intonation (your voice goes up) to show interest.</li> <li>Use falling intonation (your voice goes down) to show surprise.</li> <li>Use these techniques to keep the conversation going.</li></ul>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Showing Interest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Showing Surprise\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Oh?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Wow!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Oh, yeah?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Amazing!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Really?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Get out of here!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Oh, really?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Unbelievable!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Is that right?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"No!\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: When did you start working for the bus company?             <br><span class=\"strong\">Driver</span>: 30 years ago!            <br><span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Is that right? Amazing!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "world", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the Earth and all its countries and people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I like to meet people from around the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about daily routines.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Routines Using the Present Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Daily routines are activities you do <u>every day</u>. For example, most people would say the following  are part of their daily routine:<br>  <br>-I get up.<br> -I take a shower.<br> -I get dressed.<br> -I eat breakfast.<br> -I go to work.<br>  <br><span class=\"strong\">Note: </span>When talking about daily routines you use the <u>Simple Present tense.</u> <br>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "John doesn't wake up at 5:30 a.m.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The driver drops off his kids at school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't work on a cruise ship.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "all sorts of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "all kinds of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I get to meet all sorts of people.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "glamorous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "beautiful; lovely", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your job sounds glamorous.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "roughly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "about; approximately", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I work roughly 9 hours a day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to drop off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take someone to a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I drop off my kids at school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get a chance ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have an opportunity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I get a chance to meet many people.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With your partner, write a dialogue about each other's daily routines.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask questions about what they do every day.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 8-10 lines about daily routines.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice the dialogue and switch roles.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I ask questions about daily routines.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about my daily routines.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read dialogues aloud with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}